<title>USA: Paging Network do Brasil sell $125 mln in debt. [CORRECTED 10:15 GMT 31/5]</title>
<headline>Paging Network do Brasil sell $125 mln in debt. [CORRECTED 10:15 GMT 31/5]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following 144a private placement from Paging Network Do Brasil was priced on Friday via Merrill Lynch &amp; Co, according to market sources.</p>
<p>The notes were sold as units which also included warrants to purchase up to seven percent of the company.</p>
<p>Paging Network provides paging services in Brazil.</p>
<p>BORROWER PAGING NETWORK DO BRASIL</p>
<p>AMT $125 MLN	 COUPON 13.50 PCT  MATURITY 6/6/05</p>
<p>TYPE SR NOTES	ISS PRICE 100     FIRST PAY DATE NA</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S NR    YIELD 13.50 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>(Corrects coupon and yield from &quot;13.25 pct&quot;)</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P NR				  CALLABLE NON-CALLABLE</p>
<p>							    FOR FOUR YEARS</p>
<p>NOTES: PART OF THE PROCEEDS FROM THE OFFERING WILL BE USED TO PAY INTEREST ON THE SECURITIES FOR THE FIRST THREE-YEARS;</p>
<p>THREE-YEAR EQUITY CALL FOR 35 PERCENT OF THE ISSUE AT 113.50</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1662))</p>
